      "text": "To find the integer \\( n \\) such that \\( 0 \\leq n \\leq 7 \\) and \\( n \\equiv -3737 \\pmod{8} \\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Compute the remainder when \\(-3737\\) is divided by \\(8\\). This remainder will give us the equivalent positive integer in the range \\(0\\) to \\(7\\).\n\n2. The modulo operation works well with negative numbers as long as the result is within the desired range. Specifically, \\(-3737 \\mod 8\\) will give us the same result as \\(3737 \\mod 8\\) because both numbers modulo \\(8\\) reduce to the same residue.\n\nWe can calculate this using Python. Let's proceed with the calculation.\n```python\n# Given value\nvalue = -3737\n\n# Calculate the equivalent positive remainder\nremainder = value % 8\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n7\n```\nThe calculation \\( -3737 \\mod 8 \\) results in \\( 7 \\). Therefore, the integer \\( n \\) such that \\( 0 \\leq n \\leq 7 \\) and \\( n \\equiv -3737 \\pmod{8} \\) is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{7}\n\\]",
