      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the integer \\( n \\) such that \\( 0 \\leq n \\leq 7 \\) and \\( n \\equiv -3737 \\pmod{8} \\), we need to determine the remainder when \\( -3737 \\) is divided by \\( 8 \\). This can be done by first finding the remainder when \\( 3737 \\) is divided by \\( 8 \\), and then adjusting for the negative sign.\n\nFirst, we find the remainder of \\( 3737 \\) when divided by \\( 8 \\):\n\\[ 3737 \\div 8 = 467 \\text{ R } 1 \\]\nThis means that \\( 3737 = 8 \\cdot 467 + 1 \\), so the remainder is \\( 1 \\). Therefore,\n\\[ 3737 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{8} \\]\n\nSince \\( -3737 \\equiv -1 \\pmod{8} \\) (because \\( -1 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{8} \\) and so on),\n\\[ -3737 \\equiv -1 \\pmod{8} \\]\n\nWe need to express \\( -1 \\) in the form \\( n \\equiv a \\pmod{8} \\) where \\( 0 \\leq n \\leq 7 \\). This can be done by adding \\( 8 \\) to \\( -1 \\) until the result is in the range from \\( 0 \\) to \\( 7 \\):\n\\[ -1 + 8 = 7 - 1 = 6 \\]\nThus,\n\\[ -3737 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{8} \\]\n\nTherefore, the integer \\( n \\) is \\( 6 \\), and the final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{6} \\]",
